# Backend coding

Package: `com.expensesplit`. Layers: `controller` → `service` → `repository`; DTOs in `dto/`; entities in `entity/`.

## Patterns

- Controllers stay thin: validate, auth principal, delegate to service.
- Auth: `@AuthenticationPrincipal FirebaseUserPrincipal`.
- Mutations: `@Transactional` on service methods that write.
- Not found → `ResourceNotFoundException`; bad input → `BadRequestException` (handled globally).
- Return DTOs, never expose entities in responses.
- Amounts are INR (`BigDecimal` / decimal fields — match existing entities).

```java
// ❌ BAD — business logic in controller
@PostMapping
public GroupDto create(...) { /* persist here */ }

// ✅ GOOD
@PostMapping
@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CREATED)
public GroupDto create(@Valid @RequestBody CreateGroupRequest req,
                       @AuthenticationPrincipal FirebaseUserPrincipal principal) {
    return groupService.createGroup(req, principal);
}
```

